<article class="env-remark" id="00K7">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00K7">Remark <span data-tag="00K7">2.4.2.5</span>.</a> It follows from Corollary <a data-tag="00FY" href="/tag/00FY">1.1.5.9</a> and Remark <a data-tag="00K2" href="/tag/00K2">2.4.1.12</a> that the construction </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Cat}\rightarrow \operatorname{Cat_{\Delta }}\quad \quad \quad \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\mapsto \underline{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}_{\bullet } \]
</div>
<p> of Example <a data-tag="00K6" href="/tag/00K6">2.4.2.4</a> is fully faithful. Its essential image consists of those simplicial categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{\bullet }$ having the property that, for every pair of objects $X,Y \in \operatorname{Ob}(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{\bullet })$, the simplicial set $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}(X,Y)_{\bullet }$ is discrete (Definition <a data-tag="00FZ" href="/tag/00FZ">1.1.5.10</a>). We will sometimes abuse notation by not distinguishing between the ordinary category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and the constant simplicial category $\underline{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}_{\bullet }$. </p>
</article>
